{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119604","id":3717923167,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7dmwFf","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119604","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119604.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119604.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119604","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119604/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119604/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119604/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e458ac5a165e7bdba28a198ea13d76e9fa15ff78","number":119604,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix shader parsing of unary minus inside unbracketed math expressions","user":{"login":"KosumovicDenis","id":82704987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNzA0OTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82704987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis","html_url":"https://github.com/KosumovicDenis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KosumovicDenis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n- Closes #119576\r\n\r\nWhen passing a multiplication with a negative number not isolated in brackets to `hint_range` in the shader language, such as `instance uniform float desired : hint_range(-2.0 * PI, 2.0 * PI, 0.1) = 0.0;`, the parser throws the error `Expected a valid numeric expression.`.\r\n\r\nBased on what I could understand from the debugging, `_parse_expression` handles the AST construction. During this process, when an `OP_NEGATE` node is validated, it remains an unreduced `OperatorNode`. Therefore, when the downstream `OP_MUL` node is constructed, its left or right operand (or both) is this unreduced unary node.\r\n\r\nThen the parser passes the AST to `_reduce_expression`, but since it is limited (as the comment at line `:7897` states: `//for now only reduce simple constructors`) and does not support evaluating binary operators like `OP_MUL`, it returns the tree unreduced. This leaves the `OperatorNode` with an empty values vector, causing `_parse_numeric_constant_expression` to reject it at line `:9201`:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nif (values.is_empty()) {\r\n    return false; // To prevent possible crash.\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n*Fix:*\r\nIn `godot/servers/rendering/shader_language.cpp` within `_parse_expression` (inside the `is_unary` evaluation loop), adding a call to `_reduce_expression` immediately after a unary operator passes `_validate_operator` resolves the problem:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (!_validate_operator(p_block, p_function_info, op, &op->return_cache, &op->return_array_size)) { /* ... */ }\r\nexpression.write[i].node = _reduce_expression(p_block, expression.write[i].node); // new line\r\nexpression.remove_at(i + 1);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe intent is to achieve the same behavior of the bracketed expression (e.g., `(-2.0) * PI` works correctly because closing a parenthesis triggers an immediate reduction on its contents) by folding the unary node into a `ConstantNode` directly during the expression parsing phase.\r\n\r\n*Test:*\r\nNow shaders using `hint_range(-2.0 * PI, 2.0 * PI, 0.1)` no longer trigger parsing errors, and the slider in the Inspector is correctly populated with its minimum and maximum ranges.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues